>> title: Saba Shioyaki, Air Fryer
>> category: Smoked & Grilled
>> tags: japanese, mackerel, fish, air fryer, basket, weeknight
>> counters: The Air Fryer & the Pot
>> dish: saba-shioyaki
>> kit: Air Fryer
>> aka: さばの塩焼き, air fryer saba, salt-grilled mackerel, air fryer mackerel, saba shioyaki without a grill
>> servings: 2
>> time: 40 min
>> slack: narrow — mackerel is fat enough to forgive a minute, and two minutes past that the flesh has gone from silky to cottony
>> washing-up: the basket, the plate the fish salted on
>> keeps: not at all — cold mackerel goes cottony and the skin sags; oily fish is a same-evening thing

>> step: Written for a preheated 5.7 L basket. From cold, add three minutes. Skin side up throughout, and no turning.
The salt draws water out. Blot it off or the skin steams instead of blistering.

>> step: salt both sides and stand 20 min on a plate
Salt @mackerel fillets{2}(5 oz / 140 g each, pin-boned) on both sides with @sea salt{2%tsp} on a #plate{} and ~stand{20%min}.

>> step: pat dry, then lay skin side up in the basket
Pat @&(~1)salted mackerel{} dry with a towel and brush the skin with @sake{1%Tbs}.

>> step: roast in the basket 200°C (400°F), 10–12 min, one layer
Roast @&(~1)mackerel{} in a preheated #air fryer basket{} at 200°C (400°F) for ~air fry{11%min}, one layer and skin side up.

>> step: turn the basket at eight — skin blistered and split, fat beading
Turn @&(~1)mackerel{} in the basket without turning the fillets over.

>> step: grated daikon and soy at the table
Serve @&(~1)mackerel{} with @daikon{3%in}(grated and drained), @soy sauce{2%tsp}, @lemon{1%wedge}.
